prompts:
Use case: precise-object-edit. Asset: game animation complete character sprite atlas.
Reference image is the exact approved Mira artwork, not a redesign. Create a new transparent 4-column x 2-row atlas containing EIGHT complete left-facing Mira drawings for only the firing/recoil/settle part of her basic Bolt Shot. All 8 cells equal size, same feet/waist/head scale and fixed two-boot stance as the second-row first aim pose in reference. Draw in its same crisp, dark-outlined detailed pixel-art style.
Chronological cells left-to-right, top-to-bottom:
1 tension at fully level aim: external brass/graphite forearm cuff's small top latch pulled BACK and side plates compressed, elbow slightly bent;
2 release SNAP: latch forward/plate open by a tiny amount, forearm still level, no flame;
3 brisk recoil: cuff and wrist pull back just a little, elbow visibly folds naturally, shoulder absorbs the impulse, both boots remain fixed;
4 recoil peak: natural slightly deeper elbow bend and a one-pixel-scale shoulder compression, not whole-body translation;
5 early settle: elbow extends halfway back, plate latch resets;
6 follow-through: near aim again with tiny ponytail/strap lag;
7 lowers arm back to the reference relaxed rig hold;
8 settled relaxed rig hold matching the initial reference idle.
Her arm is intact and visible inside a WORN forearm rig, not a separate handheld gun or replacement limb. The far hand supports the cuff naturally. Exactly two arms and hands, two planted boots. Preserve dusty pink shirt, cream flower, brown short ponytail, charcoal pants, brass/graphite cuff, cyan circular emitter lens, pouch. Do NOT alter face, costume, body proportions, stance, facing or scale between cells. No projectiles, no muzzle effects, no smoke, no explosion, no text, no frames, no background, no shadows. Source is full complete drawings with ample transparent gutters. Focus on the mechanically distinct latch compression/snap and articulate elbow/shoulder recoil.
